<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kim Yu-sin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">595–673</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Kim Yushin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kim Yu-sin was a Silla general descended from the royal house of Geumgwan Gaya, his great-grandfather being its last king, Guhyeong. He led Silla's armies in the wars that destroyed Baekje in 660 and Goguryeo in 668, alliances made with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>, and supported the rise of King Muyeol. He is remembered as the chief military architect of Silla's unification of the Korean peninsula.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kim-yu-sin.jpg" alt="Kim Yu-sin" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Kim_Yushin_in_the_famous_portrait_photo_book_of_Joseon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
